      "id": "origin",
      "class": "chapter chapter-beige",
      "text": "P03 · 02 / ORIGINS & CONTINUITY How did this reading language endure? From observing time and the sky to organizing palaces, stars and inherited reading traditions, Zi Wei Dou Shu grew into a layered language of interpretation. Its reading tradition connects the structure of time with changing ways of looking at life themes. \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n \n From its roots to the present Five chapters in the development of a reading tradition 01 Astral & calendar roots Observing skies and time 02 Early chart systems Organizing chart structures 03 Palace–star synthesis Building a shared reading grammar 04 Commentary & transmission Exploring distinct commentaries 05 Modern reading Making the structure easier to read Time, palaces, stars and the tradition of interpretation ",
      "html": "<section class=\"chapter chapter-beige\" id=\"origin\"><div class=\"wrap\"><div class=\"chapter-head\"><div><div class=\"tag\">P03 · 02 / ORIGINS &amp; CONTINUITY</div><h2>How did this reading language endure?</h2><p class=\"lead\">From observing time and the sky to organizing palaces, stars and inherited reading traditions, Zi Wei Dou Shu grew into a layered language of interpretation.</p></div><p class=\"support\">Its reading tradition connects the structure of time with changing ways of looking at life themes.</p></div><figure aria-label=\"Time, palaces, stars and the tradition of interpretation\" class=\"r4-figure r4-p03\"><div class=\"r4-p03-canvas\"><svg aria-label=\"Five chapters of the history of chart reading depicted as an editorial scroll\" class=\"r4-graphic-svg\" fill=\"none\" preserveaspectratio=\"xMidYMid slice\" role=\"img\" viewbox=\"0 0 760 360\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n<defs>\n<radialgradient id=\"obsGlow\"><stop stop-color=\"#f9df9d\" stop-opacity=\".85\"></stop><stop offset=\".45\" stop-color=\"#d6b46b\" stop-opacity=\".35\"></stop><stop offset=\"1\" stop-color=\"#d6b46b\" stop-opacity=\"0\"></stop></radialgradient>\n<lineargradient id=\"goldLine\" x1=\"0\" x2=\"1\" y1=\"1\" y2=\"0\"><stop stop-color=\"#aa8140\"></stop><stop offset=\".5\" stop-color=\"#f4dc9c\"></stop><stop offset=\"1\" stop-color=\"#b99156\"></stop></lineargradient>\n<lineargradient id=\"night\" x1=\"0\" x2=\"1\" y1=\"0\" y2=\"1\"><stop stop-color=\"#101e34\"></stop><stop offset=\".55\" stop-color=\"#263c53\"></stop><stop offset=\"1\" stop-color=\"#5d6079\"></stop></lineargradient>\n<lineargradient id=\"jade\" x1=\"0\" x2=\"1\" y1=\"0\" y2=\"1\"><stop stop-color=\"#fdf9eb\"></stop><stop offset=\"1\" stop-color=\"#d5e6e3\"></stop></lineargradient>\n<filter id=\"glow\"><fegaussianblur stddeviation=\"7\"></fegaussianblur></filter>\n</defs>\n<rect fill=\"#263c4e\" height=\"360\" rx=\"25\" width=\"760\"></rect>\n<path d=\"M0 0 H760 V164 Q550 205 380 121